  cookies: "# SCHOOL Platform — Cookie Policy\n\n**Effective Date:** 1 May 2026\n**Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Are Cookies?\n\nCookies are small text files stored on your device by your browser when you visit a website. They allow the website to remember information about your visit and preferences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What Cookies We Use\n\n### 2.1 Essential Cookies (Always Active)\n\nThese cookies are necessary for the Platform to function. They cannot be disabled.\n\n| Cookie Name | Purpose | Duration |\n|---|---|---|\n| `school_session` | Maintains your authenticated login session | 7 days |\n| `school_csrf` | Protects against Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks | 7 days |\n| `lite_mode` | Remembers your bandwidth/data-saving preference | 1 year |\n\n### 2.2 Preference Cookies (Optional)\n\nThese cookies remember your settings and preferences.\n\n| Cookie Name | Purpose | Duration |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` | Stores your display theme preference | 1 year |\n\n### 2.3 Analytics Cookies (Optional — Consent Required)\n\nThese cookies help us understand how the Platform is used. We activate these only with your consent.\n\n| Cookie Name | Provider | Purpose | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| None currently | No analytics provider in use | Not applicable — platform does not currently use analytics cookies | N/A |\n\n### 2.4 Third-Party Cookies\n\nOur payment processor (Stripe) may set cookies during the checkout flow. These are governed by Stripe's Cookie Policy at https://stripe.com/za/cookie-settings.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Your Cookie Choices\n\n### 3.1 Cookie Consent Banner\n\nWhen you first visit the Platform, you will be presented with a consent banner allowing you to accept or decline optional cookies. Essential cookies are always active.\n\n### 3.2 Withdrawing Consent\n\nYou may withdraw cookie consent at any time:\n- Through the **Cookie Preferences** link in the Platform footer; or\n- By clearing cookies in your browser settings (note: this will log you out of your session).\n\n### 3.3 Browser Controls\n\nMost browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings. Visit your browser's help documentation for instructions.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Zero-Rated Endpoints\n\nCertain Platform endpoints are designated as **zero-rated** under ICASA data zero-rating guidelines for educational content:\n\n- `/api/lesson-json`\n- `/api/lessons/quiz/bias`\n- `/api/lessons/quiz/attempt`\n\nThese endpoints operate without cookies where technically feasible to minimise data usage on mobile networks.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Cookie Policy when we add or remove cookies. Material changes will be notified through the Platform's cookie consent mechanism.\n\n---\n\n*DITSHEGO VENTURES (Pty) Ltd t/a SCHOOL — legal@school.ditshego-ventures.co.za*\n\n*Last reviewed: 1 May 2026*\n",
  aup: "# SCHOOL Platform — Acceptable Use Policy\n\n**Effective Date:** 1 May 2026\n**Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis Acceptable Use Policy (\"**AUP**\") defines the rules governing how you may use the SCHOOL Platform. By using the Platform you agree to this AUP. Violations may result in suspension or termination of your account.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Permitted Uses\n\nYou may use the Platform to:\n- Study curriculum-aligned learning content for personal academic improvement;\n- Practise past papers and review marked attempts;\n- Interact with the AI study assistant for educational purposes;\n- Book and attend tutoring sessions with registered tutors;\n- Participate in community discussion rooms for academic support;\n- Manage your personal study planner and academic schedule.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Prohibited Uses\n\n### 3.1 Academic Dishonesty\n\nYou may not use the Platform to:\n- Submit AI-generated answers to formal school assessments as your own work where your school prohibits such use (check your institution's AI policy);\n- Share past paper solutions with others in a manner that facilitates cheating in formal assessments;\n- Access restricted examination content ahead of formal release;\n- Assist others in academic dishonesty.\n\nSCHOOL promotes legitimate study practice. We are not responsible for disciplinary actions imposed by schools or examination bodies arising from a user's misuse of Platform content.\n\n### 3.2 Illegal Activity\n\nYou may not use the Platform to:\n- Engage in any activity that violates South African law or the law of your jurisdiction;\n- Distribute, sell, or otherwise commercialise DBE past papers, CAPS materials, or SCHOOL content without authorisation;\n- Circumvent geographic access restrictions or payment controls;\n- Engage in money laundering or financial fraud through the wallet system.\n\n### 3.3 Harmful Content\n\nYou may not post or transmit content that:\n- Is defamatory, harassing, threatening, or discriminatory on grounds of race, gender, religion, disability, sexual orientation, or any other ground prohibited by the **Promotion of Equality and Prevention of Unfair Discrimination Act 4 of 2000**;\n- Is sexually explicit or pornographic;\n- Depicts violence or glorifies harm;\n- Targets minors in any inappropriate way.\n\n### 3.4 Privacy and Data\n\nYou may not:\n- Share another person's personal information without their consent;\n- Scrape, harvest, or aggregate personal information from the Platform;\n- Impersonate another user, SCHOOL staff member, or any third party;\n- Attempt to identify, de-anonymise, or contact other users outside the Platform's messaging system for purposes other than legitimate tutoring.\n\n### 3.5 Technical Interference\n\nYou may not:\n- Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the Platform or its infrastructure;\n- Conduct denial-of-service attacks, penetration testing, or security scanning against the Platform without SCHOOL's written consent;\n- Reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Platform software;\n- Introduce malware, viruses, or malicious code;\n- Use automated bots, scripts, or scrapers to interact with the Platform.\n\n### 3.6 Tutor Marketplace Abuse\n\nYou may not:\n- Book tutoring sessions with no intention of attending;\n- Submit false disputes or ratings;\n- Attempt to route payments for tutoring services outside the Platform to circumvent SCHOOL's commission;\n- Use the tutor messaging system for spam or commercial solicitation unrelated to tutoring.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Content Standards\n\nAll content you submit must:\n- Be truthful and not misleading;\n- Comply with applicable copyright law (see the **Copyright and Content Policy**);\n- Be appropriate for a platform used by students of all ages from Grade R (approximately 5 years) through Grade 12 (approximately 18 years).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Tutor-Specific Standards\n\nTutors must additionally:\n- Hold genuine qualifications relevant to the subjects they offer;\n- Not make false claims about qualifications or experience;\n- Treat all learners with respect regardless of their academic level;\n- Maintain professional conduct during sessions;\n- Comply with all applicable laws regarding the provision of educational services to minors.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Reporting Violations\n\nIf you observe content or behaviour that violates this AUP, report it to: support@school.ditshego-ventures.co.za or use the in-platform report function.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Consequences of Violation\n\nViolations of this AUP may result in:\n- Content removal;\n- Warning issued to your account;\n- Temporary suspension;\n- Permanent account termination;\n- Forfeiture of wallet credits without refund (for fraud or abuse);\n- Referral to law enforcement where required by law.\n\nSCHOOL will apply these consequences proportionately and in accordance with the Terms of Service.\n\n---\n\n*DITSHEGO VENTURES (Pty) Ltd t/a SCHOOL — [Redacted for public repository — contact privacy@ditshego-ventures.co.za] — support@school.ditshego-ventures.co.za*\n\n*Last reviewed: 1 May 2026*\n",
